MARGIN: should print same text with different margins.
(0,0)
MARGIN sets the left margin and right margin in pixels.  Left and right are the
widths of the margins, not the locations of the margins, so both are initially
0.  The margins are stored in the LMRG and RMRG words of the interpreter.
(10,10)
MARGIN sets the left margin and right margin in pixels.
Left and right are the widths of the margins, not the
locations of the margins, so both are initially 0.  The
margins are stored in the LMRG and RMRG words of the
interpreter.
